==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|шкап}}

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|ru|gem-pro|*skapą}}. The form {{m|ru||шкап}} is from {{der|ru|dum|-}} and/or {{der|ru|gml|schap}} (both “cupboard, cabinet, coffer”). The form {{m|ru||шкаф}} was likely influenced by the {{cog|gmh|-}} cognate {{m|gmh|schaf}} (whence {{cog|pl|szafa}}). The initial ''шк-'' seems to speak against direct borrowing from High German, where ''sch-'' was pronounced {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}} early on; on the other hand compare {{cog|sh|шкаф}}.

